WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.220 --> 00:00:01.480
The question that we have

00:00:01.480 --> 00:00:04.660
before us is when

00:00:04.660 --> 00:00:06.900
do the divisions between

00:00:06.900 --> 00:00:07.846
us and them,

00:00:07.846 --> 00:00:09.440
when is that productive?

00:00:09.440 --> 00:00:10.580
When is that something

00:00:10.580 --> 00:00:13.030
that really helps our
societies?

00:00:13.030 --> 00:00:14.600
And in what cases does

00:00:14.600 --> 00:00:16.720
it become really problematic

00:00:16.720 --> 00:00:17.680
and how can we overcome

00:00:17.680 --> 00:00:19.019
those problems and

00:00:19.019 --> 00:00:20.920
maybe reconfigure the we

00:00:20.920 --> 00:00:22.900
and the them, or
at least see them

00:00:22.900 --> 00:00:25.000
not in an antagonistic way,

00:00:25.000 --> 00:00:26.240
or a threatening way,

00:00:26.240 --> 00:00:28.220
but in a way that's
complimentary,

00:00:28.220 --> 00:00:29.460
or that we can live

00:00:29.460 --> 00:00:31.069
in co-existence.

00:00:31.069 --> 00:00:32.280
That historically the ways

00:00:32.280 --> 00:00:34.400
in which states,
and governments,

00:00:34.400 --> 00:00:35.220
and societies have tried

00:00:35.220 --> 00:00:39.620
to construct these feelings of trust,

00:00:39.620 --> 00:00:42.780
and solidarity is by

00:00:42.780 --> 00:00:44.340
defining out-groups.

00:00:44.340 --> 00:00:46.400
So we build in-group solidarity

00:00:46.400 --> 00:00:49.078
by distinguishing ourselves as different from

00:00:49.078 --> 00:00:49.970
and better than

00:00:49.970 --> 00:00:52.980
others and in today's world that

00:00:52.980 --> 00:00:54.540
strategy is just-

00:00:54.540 --> 00:00:57.360
it's dangerous, and it's self-defeating.

00:00:57.360 --> 00:01:03.610
As a matter of public policy, of concerned
citizens, of people of the world we want to

00:01:03.610 --> 00:01:07.870
understand how we can build a more inclusive
and just society.

00:01:07.870 --> 00:01:13.500
What CIFAR allows, and I think this is unique
really to CIFAR is it allows a group of people

00:01:13.500 --> 00:01:22.190
who share interests to spend some time together
to figure out how to talk to each other, how

00:01:22.190 --> 00:01:28.800
to draw links with each other and then...

00:01:28.800 --> 00:01:32.780
be able to design some more specific collaborative

00:01:32.780 --> 00:01:33.860
research projects.

00:01:33.860 --> 00:01:42.040
If we can better understand how to mitigate
the negative consequences of seeing someone

00:01:42.040 --> 00:01:49.360
as an other potentially blur the boundaries
between groups, maybe sometimes erase those

00:01:49.360 --> 00:01:56.909
boundaries, or recognize that people are different
but that we can still work together in collective

00:01:56.909 --> 00:02:03.240
projects to increase the rights and resources
that everybody has I think will make our world

00:02:03.240 --> 00:02:04.240
a better place.

00:02:04.240 --> 00:02:04.241
[Music]

